[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3725040394","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114754#issuecomment-3725040394","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114754","id":3725040394,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eB5sK","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-08T18:04:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T18:06:05Z","body":"This is an interesting idea, but I think showing the UTC time alone is enough (so it's more compact). If you really want to show local time, perhaps it should be done on the same line after UTC time.\r\n\r\nAll in all, I would try to compact the display from 3 lines to just 1. Maybe you can even put this information on the same line as \"Time elapsed\" as follows:\r\n\r\n> INFO: Time elapsed: 00:00:20.05 (build ended at 2026-01-08 14:49:26 UTC)\r\n\r\nI would also clean up the timestamp a little to be more readable (remove milliseconds, and replace `T` with a space).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3725040394/rea